{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0113DY9SwmLUkcZBvB8akvRK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Codebase improve skill ran. Critical eval of Explore agent findings:\n\n**Finding 1 (almanac-core.sh \"shallow wrapper\")** — REJECT. Owns skill-metadata validation contract; tests/install/sync share it. CLAUDE.md mandates skill-format helpers live there. Deletion scatters validation across N callers. Earns its keep.\n\n**Finding 2 (converge-core complexity → reusable parse_structured_response)** — REJECT. Converge parser is 4-field state-machine (VERDICT/REASON/STEER/GOAL_UPDATE w/ markdown-decoration tolerance, partial-output policy). Purpose-built for the overseer contract. No other loop has that shape.\n\n**Finding 3 (temp file pattern across 22 sites)** — MARGINAL. All sites use `${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/almanac-X.XXXXXX` uniformly, paired with local `rm -f`. No leak hazard (`agent_capture` itself doesn't trap-create temps for callers). Centralizing saves ~1 literal substring per site, doesn't concentrate real complexity. Deletion test fails: a `_almanac_mktemp` wrapper IS itself shallow.\n\n**Finding 4 (unified freeform parser)** — REJECT (factually wrong). Harden's verdict parser is `grep -Fxq 'HARDEN_VERDICT=reproduces'` (single-token). Converge's is multi-field state-machine. Different problems, no parallel pattern to unify.\n\n**Finding 5 (worker schema mirrors run schema)** — REJECT. Both already use the same deep engine `almanac_loop_tsv_record_set`. The two field-list functions are intentional per CONTEXT.md (\"worker.sh owns worker-status record schema, uses run.sh's engine\"). Moving them together would couple write-orchestration (worker.sh) to registry-read (run.sh). Boundary is correct.\n\n## Verdict\n\nCodebase **converged**. No findings pass the deletion test. Architecture has matured through prior converge rounds (loop adapters, provider adapters, slug, agent_capture/stream/raw, role resolution,